{"id": "q0032", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1851623335, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "It takes John 5 minutes to get to the first side of the Rubik's cube.  The second and third sides each take twice that long.  The last 2 sides each take half as long as the first, and once you get the 5th side you have all 6 sides.  How long does the Rubik's cube take?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0032.wav", "input_sha256": "dd6bb8eaf3ba4d96a20484261431d205031c7d63946e979d8a2fd7d9fc942c2e", "input_samples": 330400, "input_s": 20.65, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.3343, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "First side: 5 minutes Second side: twice as long as first: 2 × 5 = 10 minutes Third side: twice as long as first: 2 × 5 = 10 minutes Fourth side: half as long as first: 5 ÷ 2 = 2.5 minutes Fifth side: half as long as first: 5 ÷ 2 = 2.5 minutes Once the fifth side is done, all six sides are complete, so there is no separate sixth side time. Total: 5 + 10 + 10 + 2.5 + 2.5 = 30 Final numeric answer: 30 minutes", "expert_answer": "First side: **5 minutes**\n\nSecond side: twice as long as first:  \n**2 × 5 = 10 minutes**\n\nThird side: twice as long as first:  \n**2 × 5 = 10 minutes**\n\nFourth side: half as long as first:  \n**5 ÷ 2 = 2.5 minutes**\n\nFifth side: half as long as first:  \n**5 ÷ 2 = 2.5 minutes**\n\nOnce the fifth side is done, all six sides are complete, so there is no separate sixth side time.\n\nTotal:  \n**5 + 10 + 10 + 2.5 + 2.5 = 30**\n\n**Final numeric answer: 30 minutes**", "transcript": "It takes John five minutes to get to the first side of the Rubik's Cube. The second and third sides each take twice that long. The last two sides each take half as long as the first, and once you get the fifth side, you have all six sides. How long does the Rubik's Cube take? Show your work and end ", "asr_s": 1.11, "expert_s": 4.65, "expert_input_samples": 330400, "expert_input_s": 20.65, "expert_input_sha256": "dd6bb8eaf3ba4d96a20484261431d205031c7d63946e979d8a2fd7d9fc942c2e", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.325, "relay_synth_ms": 18379, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 367, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 367, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0032_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "fce9e21827dbcd42e26e8983f598ab9397a540ae7c42a0722259019342cf98ed", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 30.32}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0032_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "a6ebebb00c5b9cb2b8e878cffbdf4ce2b14ab52aa37121bae5626bbdd7e8a9d0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0032_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "3f74d040dac3ec52f2e6764028a5903a3cf2f87d989267c6e586fca6e18598ab", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.077, 1.141, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.079, 2.143, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.075, 3.134, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.075, 4.132, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.076, 5.136, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.074, 6.131, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.075, 7.134, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.075, 8.133, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.079, 9.14, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.077, 10.14, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.076, 11.137, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.077, 12.138, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.076, 13.134, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.083, 14.142, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.082, 15.144, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.078, 16.136, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.082, 17.143, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.085, 18.153, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.082, 19.143, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.078, 20.138, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 20.65, 20.728, 21.403, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.65, 22.089, 22.844, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 20.65, "last_real_feed_done": 20.728, "onset": 21.403, "gate_read_done": 21.403, "fire": 21.403, "candidate_first_pcm": 21.403, "stall_note": 21.406, "stall_first_pcm": 22.017, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 22.844, "expert_req": 21.405, "expert_resp": 27.169, "relay_synth_start": 27.169, "relay_first_pcm": 27.977, "relay_synth_end": 45.548, "first_any_pcm": 21.403, "first_answer_pcm": 27.977, "session_end": 45.762}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.327, "ttfa_any_s": 0.753}
{"id": "q0046", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 644994425, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Tim wanted to make lemonade for a pool party.  For a gallon of lemonade, his recipe called for 1 cup of fresh lemon juice.  He found that 6 lemons would yield 1 cup of juice.  He figured he would need to make 4 gallons of lemonade for the party.  His best friend Allen asked if Tim could make an extra gallon for him that was twice as tart as the other gallons.  How many lemons will Tim need?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0046.wav", "input_sha256": "32303a4d2647ea70e6aa653b6863131143cb196357ca08a522c9ca79b95a6459", "input_samples": 453200, "input_s": 28.325, "n_real_chunks": 29, "score": 0.4403, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "For 1 gallon of lemonade: Recipe needs 1 cup of lemon juice. , 6 lemons yield 1 cup of juice. Tim needs: 4 gallons for the party: \\(4 \\times 1 = 4\\) cups of lemon juice Alan wants: 1 extra gallon that is twice as tart, so it needs: \\(2 \\times 1 = 2\\) cups of lemon juice Total lemon juice needed: \\[ 4 + 2 = 6 \\text{ cups} \\] Since each cup requires 6 lemons: \\[ 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\] Final numeric answer: 36", "expert_answer": "For 1 gallon of lemonade:\n\n- Recipe needs **1 cup** of lemon juice.\n- **6 lemons** yield **1 cup** of juice.\n\nTim needs:\n\n- **4 gallons** for the party:  \n  \\(4 \\times 1 = 4\\) cups of lemon juice\n\nAlan wants:\n\n- **1 extra gallon** that is **twice as tart**, so it needs:  \n  \\(2 \\times 1 = 2\\) cups of lemon juice\n\nTotal lemon juice needed:\n\n\\[\n4 + 2 = 6 \\text{ cups}\n\\]\n\nSince each cup requires 6 lemons:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 6 = 36\n\\]\n\n**Final numeric answer: 36**", "transcript": "Tim wanted to make lemonade for a pool party. For a gallon of lemonade, his recipe called for one cup of fresh lemon juice. He found that six lemons would yield one cup of juice. He figured he would need to make four gallons of lemonade for the party. His best friend Alan asked if Tim could make an ", "asr_s": 1.4, "expert_s": 4.47, "expert_input_samples": 453200, "expert_input_s": 28.325, "expert_input_sha256": "32303a4d2647ea70e6aa653b6863131143cb196357ca08a522c9ca79b95a6459", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.539, "relay_synth_ms": 24869, "onset_chunk": 28, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 471, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 471, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0046_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "5e63165f07125f5b64ac84b7697eec82b99ff15db0660b26ae9720bca0a7a9d1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 43.52}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0046_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "de5d48a3a02aba87278bd8e9f17126666b49cdb842a6d3bf3da3ab070d17f7f5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0046_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "a74f826c4f822ec6ce94236d22dfbe7c724b02e9f191fc7b3139b6d92d821a90", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.24}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.073, 1.133, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.078, 2.14, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.075, 3.132, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.08, 4.144, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.085, 5.146, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.079, 6.142, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.08, 7.142, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.079, 8.14, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.083, 9.144, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.078, 10.139, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.077, 11.135, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.079, 12.14, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.079, 13.139, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.078, 14.138, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.079, 15.138, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.076, 16.134, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 1