{"id": "q0410", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3043765461, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "What is fleece?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0410.wav", "input_sha256": "c3e1d38e3f1e617343fbabbc09619d7beb2916e430666ff8ea2f22d8ed38cea5", "input_samples": 14600, "input_s": 0.912, "n_real_chunks": 1, "score": 0.8137, "act": 0.9908, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Fleece can mean: The woolly coat of a sheep or similar animal, especially after it has been sheared. , A soft, warm fabric often made from synthetic fibers like polyester, used in jackets, blankets, and outdoor clothing. , As a verb, to fleece someone means to cheat or overcharge them.", "expert_answer": "**Fleece** can mean:\n\n1. **The woolly coat of a sheep or similar animal**, especially after it has been sheared.\n2. **A soft, warm fabric** often made from synthetic fibers like polyester, used in jackets, blankets, and outdoor clothing.\n3. As a verb, **to fleece someone** means to cheat or overcharge them.", "transcript": "What is fleece?\n", "asr_s": 0.62, "expert_s": 2.32, "expert_input_samples": 14600, "expert_input_s": 0.912, "expert_input_sha256": "c3e1d38e3f1e617343fbabbc09619d7beb2916e430666ff8ea2f22d8ed38cea5", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.448, "relay_synth_ms": 10353, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 199, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 199, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0410_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "37c15523459ab57ee5f1656785084555a23b568f08eca27ae6883df87850f738", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 17.76}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0410_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "2a92616226ee07dbe46e58c5cefe67cdffe7fa974eaa3ac01a564bcccf09ee90", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0410_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "30c322d20dabbc155361a90f961d5a5f865bf85cc1fb946e4dcdf88d236faa6b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 0.912, 0.986, 1.044, 1, 0, 0], [1, 0, 1.913, 1.986, 2.045, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.913, 2.988, 3.046, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.913, 3.989, 4.482, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.912, 5.19, 5.97, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 0.912, "last_real_feed_done": 0.986, "onset": 4.482, "gate_read_done": 4.482, "fire": 4.482, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.482, "stall_note": 4.483, "stall_first_pcm": 5.112, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.97, "expert_req": 4.483, "expert_resp": 7.417, "relay_synth_start": 7.418, "relay_first_pcm": 8.241, "relay_synth_end": 17.772, "first_any_pcm": 4.482, "first_answer_pcm": 8.241, "session_end": 17.952}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.328, "ttfa_any_s": 3.57}
{"id": "q0430", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2270842455, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Why do people like to buy Apple products?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0430.wav", "input_sha256": "4c1ec7450720ff60c2e64c53b6e145928bf04b30f77ab3fe34356ee9ae7570a1", "input_samples": 38400, "input_s": 2.4, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.3423, "act": 0.9976, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "People like to buy Apple products for several reasons: Ease of use: Apple devices are known for simple, intuitive interfaces. , Ecosystem integration: iPhone, Mac, iPad, Apple Watch, AirPods, and iCloud work smoothly together. , Design and build quality: Many users value Apple’s sleek design, materials, and attention to detail. , Brand reputation: Apple is associated with quality, innovation, and.", "expert_answer": "People like to buy Apple products for several reasons:\n\n- **Ease of use:** Apple devices are known for simple, intuitive interfaces.\n- **Ecosystem integration:** iPhone, Mac, iPad, Apple Watch, AirPods, and iCloud work smoothly together.\n- **Design and build quality:** Many users value Apple’s sleek design, materials, and attention to detail.\n- **Brand reputation:** Apple is associated with quality, innovation, and status.\n- **Privacy and security:** Apple markets strong privacy protections and long software support.\n- **App and accessory support:** Apple products have a large ecosystem of apps, cases, chargers, and services.\n- **Customer service:** Apple Stores, repairs, and support are convenient in many places.\n- **Resale value:** Apple devices often retain value better than many competing products.\n\nIn short, people often buy Apple products because they are polished, reliable, easy to use, and work well together.", "transcript": "Why do people like to buy Apple products?\n", "asr_s": 0.65, "expert_s": 4.94, "expert_input_samples": 38400, "expert_input_s": 2.4, "expert_input_sha256": "4c1ec7450720ff60c2e64c53b6e145928bf04b30f77ab3fe34356ee9ae7570a1", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.12, "relay_synth_ms": 15951, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 447, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 447, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0430_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "016b0ee0ab807a4ff96ad1b3e320275e3a949b15f119b2760f4d4b74db32c19a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 28.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0430_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "a13114421589e46a3a70c59e5326d4bfe99af5f1a731f95eb3de0f78c7395775", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0430_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "b9064641db213450a3a31db516cffa25349d93579cf53a2e2b9628e5b453e9d2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.073, 1.132, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.075, 2.135, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.4, 2.476, 2.534, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.4, 3.475, 4.225, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.4, 4.929, 5.699, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.4, "last_real_feed_done": 2.476, "onset": 4.225, "gate_read_done": 4.225, "fire": 4.225, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.225, "stall_note": 4.226, "stall_first_pcm": 4.848, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.699, "expert_req": 4.226, "expert_resp": 9.819, "relay_synth_start": 9.819, "relay_first_pcm": 10.637, "relay_synth_end": 25.771, "first_any_pcm": 4.225, "first_answer_pcm": 10.637, "session_end": 25.969}, "ttfa_answer_s": 8.237, "ttfa_any_s": 1.825}
{"id": "q0456", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 946031844, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "How can I sleep well at night?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0456.wav", "input_sha256": "793ccb8e311490b330e6c7141f007d5d8c11b837cf9fc980021c27f6423c0518", "input_samples": 29200, "input_s": 1.825, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.3848, "act": 0.9888, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "To sleep well at night, try these evidence-based habits: Keep a consistent schedule: Go to bed and wake up at about the same time every day, even weekends. , Get morning light: Sunlight soon after waking helps regulate your body clock. , Limit caffeine and nicotine: Avoid caffeine in the afternoon/evening. , Avoid heavy meals and alcohol close to bedtime: Alcohol may make you sleepy but often.", "expert_answer": "To sleep well at night, try these evidence-based habits:\n\n- **Keep a consistent schedule:** Go to bed and wake up at about the same time every day, even weekends.\n- **Get morning light:** Sunlight soon after waking helps regulate your body clock.\n- **Limit caffeine and nicotine:** Avoid caffeine in the afternoon/evening.\n- **Avoid heavy meals and alcohol close to bedtime:** Alcohol may make you sleepy but often worsens sleep quality.\n- **Create a wind-down routine:** Read, stretch, meditate, or take a warm shower 30–60 minutes before bed.\n- **Make your room sleep-friendly:** Cool, dark, quiet, and comfortable.\n- **Reduce screens before bed:** Dim lights and avoid phones/computers for the last 30–60 minutes if possible.\n- **Use the bed only for sleep and sex:** This helps your brain associate bed with sleep.\n- **If you can’t sleep after ~20 minutes:** Get up, do something quiet in dim light, and return when sleepy.\n- **Exercise regularly:** But avoid intense workouts right before bed.\n\nIf poor sleep lasts **more than a few weeks**, or you snore loudly, gasp for air, feel very sleepy during the day, or have anxiety/depression symptoms, consider talking with a healthcare professional.", "transcript": "How can I sleep well at night?\n", "asr_s": 0.79, "expert_s": 5.56, "expert_input_samples": 29200, "expert_input_s": 1.825, "expert_input_sha256": "793ccb8e311490b330e6c7141f007d5d8c11b837cf9fc980021c27f6423c0518", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.555, "relay_synth_ms": 12754, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0456_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "59362ad05d84116433c1638e4ad17145a143667ded06a5ecea6c74baeeceaec8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 22.32}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0456_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "8b303a94ec87e5f27b6152eebc043261febfdd9a96acff3cefece6b4456065a0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0456_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "411f48582ffb9bb4438cc66943fe50e0a2fd24020cef73f9cfad58b05dec64c8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.074, 1.134, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.825, 1.898, 1.956, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.825, 2.899, 2.956, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.825, 3.898, 4.573, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.825, "last_real_feed_done": 1.898, "onset": 4.573, "gate_read_done": 4.574, "fire": 4.574, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.573, "stall_note": 4.574, "stall_first_pcm": 5.378, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.378, "expert_req": 4.574, "expert_resp": 10.933, "relay_synth_start": 10.934, "relay_first_pcm": 11.759, "relay_synth_end": 23.688, "first_any_pcm": 4.573, "first_answer_pcm": 11.759, "session_end": 23.879}, "ttfa_answer_s": 9.934, "ttfa_any_s": 2.748}
{"id": "q0469", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2213610166, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "What are some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0469.wav", "input_sha256": "a81229068e18c78097f4aa739684251b9b0beffb4178c6319a12e2e3fad7cc89", "input_samples": 54600, "input_s": 3.413, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.3917, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup: A measuring jug , A tiny flowerpot — clean and unused , A ladle , A hollowed-out pineapple , A soup bowl , A watering can — clean and food-safe , A teapot spout-first , A plastic beach bucket , A mason jar with a comically long straw , A clean rubber boot — as a joke, not recommended , A helmet , A trophy , A hollowed watermelon , A vase — clean and safe glass only , A gravy boat , A laboratory beaker — only if food-safe and never used for chemicals , A giant seashell-shaped bowl , A dog bowl — new and washed , A coconut shell , A pitcher you refuse to pour from", "expert_answer": "Some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup:\n\n- A **measuring jug**\n- A **tiny flowerpot** — clean and unused\n- A **ladle**\n- A **hollowed-out pineapple**\n- A **soup bowl**\n- A **watering can** — clean and food-safe\n- A **teapot spout-first**\n- A **plastic beach bucket**\n- A **mason jar with a comically long straw**\n- A **clean rubber boot** — as a joke, not recommended\n- A **helmet**\n- A **trophy**\n- A **hollowed watermelon**\n- A **vase** — clean and safe glass only\n- A **gravy boat**\n- A **laboratory beaker** — only if food-safe and never used for chemicals\n- A **giant seashell-shaped bowl**\n- A **dog bowl** — new and washed\n- A **coconut shell**\n- A **pitcher you refuse to pour from**", "transcript": "What are some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup?\n", "asr_s": 0.78, "expert_s": 5.17, "expert_input_samples": 54600, "expert_input_s": 3.413, "expert_input_sha256": "a81229068e18c78097f4aa739684251b9b0beffb4178c6319a12e2e3fad7cc89", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.734, "relay_synth_ms": 27848, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 2, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 2, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0469_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "fd1a7604e58dcd64cbe217040afbf8189adf4794a24adbca420bfe457fba1aa1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 48.88}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0469_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "3836d51c2954f368723ac752786e6ad84456cc5b62adda9a9f6d73706e09ad96", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.12}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.074, 1.132, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.074, 2.132, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.076, 3.135, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.413, 3.486, 3.792, 0, 0, 0], [4, 0, 4.412, 4.488, 5.005, 0, 26880, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.413, "last_real_feed_done": 3.486, "onset": 3.792, "gate_read_done": 3.792, "fire": 3.792, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "stall_note": 3.793, "stall_first_pcm": 4.414, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.005, "expert_req": 3.793, "expert_resp": 9.739, "relay_synth_start": 9.739, "relay_first_pcm": 10.562, "relay_synth_end": 37.588, "first_any_pcm": 4.414, "first_answer_pcm": 10.562, "session_end": 37.842}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.149, "ttfa_any_s": 1.002}
{"id": "q0489", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 494022456, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "我去了他们的房子，但是没有人在家。", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0489.wav", "input_sha256": "31c084909b975d36ccce199c7fa0fd1a0600135a7bbe792b0284311557a57c09", "input_samples": 52600, "input_s": 3.288, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.7305, "act": 0.9857, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "英文可译为： I went to their house, but no one was home.", "expert_answer": "英文可译为：\n\n**I went to their house, but no one was home.**", "transcript": "我去了他们的房子，但是没有人在家。\n", "asr_s": 0.85, "expert_s": 1.49, "expert_input_samples": 52600, "expert_input_s": 3.288, "expert_input_sha256": "31c084909b975d36ccce199c7fa0fd1a0600135a7bbe792b0284311557a57c09", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.527, "relay_synth_ms": 2747, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0489_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "0d7ed64aecdad136769037672540084706cf4798665179565fe3b7569ffff6eb", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 4.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0489_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "ea0afc5968184285cf896c88cbb88e86317687a21bec826b681cde4770757dca", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0489_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "dc3ebcd01b666a16534226ee8627fb948716d69f826e8888666095acfa8c7a20", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.072, 1.129, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.078, 2.136, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.077, 3.133, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.288, 3.363, 4.122, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.288, "last_real_feed_done": 3.363, "onset": 4.122, "gate_read_done": 4.123, "fire": 4.123, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.122, "stall_note": 4.124, "stall_first_pcm": 4.935, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.935, "expert_req": 4.123, "expert_resp": 6.461, "relay_synth_start": 6.462, "relay_first_pcm": 7.305, "relay_synth_end": 9.21, "first_any_pcm": 4.122, "first_answer_pcm": 7.305, "session_end": 9.352}, "ttfa_answer_s": 4.018, "ttfa_any_s": 0.835}
{"id": "q0501", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3669116725, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "公司可以引入哪些新流程来减少碳足迹？", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0501.wav", "input_sha256": "1883cae31df935234da82dd60d4701d237119c158ea51d8c2eb06b60452b44e0", "input_samples": 62400, "input_s": 3.9, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.4138, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "公司可引入以下流程来减少碳足迹： , 碳盘查流程 定期统计办公、生产、运输、采购等环节的碳排放，建立基准数据。 , 能源管理流程 监测用电、用气、用水情况，设定节能目标，推广高效照明、空调优化和设备节能运行。 , 绿色采购流程 优先选择低碳、可回收、环保认证的原材料、设备和供应商。 , 供应链碳管理流程 要求供应商披露碳排放数据，并将低碳表现纳入供应商评估标准。 , 低碳生产流程 优化工艺，减少能源消耗、废料和排放，推动循环利用和清洁生产。 , 废弃物分类与回收流程 建立纸张、塑料、金属、电子废弃物等分类回收机制，减少填埋和焚烧。 , 绿色办公流程 推行无纸化办公、远程会议、节能设备、办公区域温控标准等措施。 , 低碳出行流程 鼓励员工使用公共交通、拼车、骑行、电动车，并减少不必要差旅。 , 产品生命周期评估流程 从设计、生产、运输、使用到报废，评估并降低产品全生命周期碳排放。 , 碳目标与绩效考核流程 设定年度减排目标，将节能减排指标纳入部门和管理层绩效考核。 , 员工培训与参与流程 定期开展低碳培训，鼓励员工提出节能减排改进建议。 , 可再生能源采购流程 逐步使用太阳能、风电、绿电证书或长期绿色电力采购协议。 最有效的做法是先进行碳盘查，找出主要排放来源，再针对能源、供应链、生产和运输等重点环节制定减排流程。", "expert_answer": "公司可引入以下流程来减少碳足迹：\n\n1. **碳盘查流程**  \n   定期统计办公、生产、运输、采购等环节的碳排放，建立基准数据。\n\n2. **能源管理流程**  \n   监测用电、用气、用水情况，设定节能目标，推广高效照明、空调优化和设备节能运行。\n\n3. **绿色采购流程**  \n   优先选择低碳、可回收、环保认证的原材料、设备和供应商。\n\n4. **供应链碳管理流程**  \n   要求供应商披露碳排放数据，并将低碳表现纳入供应商评估标准。\n\n5. **低碳生产流程**  \n   优化工艺，减少能源消耗、废料和排放，推动循环利用和清洁生产。\n\n6. **废弃物分类与回收流程**  \n   建立纸张、塑料、金属、电子废弃物等分类回收机制，减少填埋和焚烧。\n\n7. **绿色办公流程**  \n   推行无纸化办公、远程会议、节能设备、办公区域温控标准等措施。\n\n8. **低碳出行流程**  \n   鼓励员工使用公共交通、拼车、骑行、电动车，并减少不必要差旅。\n\n9. **产品生命周期评估流程**  \n   从设计、生产、运输、使用到报废，评估并降低产品全生命周期碳排放。\n\n10. **碳目标与绩效考核流程**  \n   设定年度减排目标，将节能减排指标纳入部门和管理层绩效考核。\n\n11. **员工培训与参与流程**  \n   定期开展低碳培训，鼓励员工提出节能减排改进建议。\n\n12. **可再生能源采购流程**  \n   逐步使用太阳能、风电、绿电证书或长期绿色电力采购协议。\n\n最有效的做法是先进行**碳盘查**，找出主要排放来源，再针对能源、供应链、生产和运输等重点环节制定减排流程。", "transcript": "公司可以引入哪些新流程来减少碳足迹？\n", "asr_s": 0.66, "expert_s": 9.57, "expert_input_samples": 62400, "expert_input_s": 3.9, "expert_input_sha256": "1883cae31df935234da82dd60d4701d237119c158ea51d8c2eb06b60452b44e0", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 8.943, "relay_synth_ms": 67841, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 204, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 204, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0501_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "5338b64d366196579449d1c2090a2390468ec28a621fe7eaae9539a6d775de43", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 118.2}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0501_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "babc2908e3dccd448e548d5a7d4791025cb6faf53ce1f0e4cef7b9c1939eb6d4", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0501_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "b45299892f6bcf2635137d79e86f30943796914a5ce00eabfb69ffce60f6a87a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.24}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.075, 1.134, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.075, 2.133, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.078, 3.135, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.9, 3.977, 4.038, 1, 0, 0], [4, 0, 4.9, 4.976, 5.496, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.9, 6.183, 6.786, 0, 29760, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.9, "last_real_feed_done": 3.977, "onset": 5.496, "gate_read_done": 5.496, "fire": 5.496, "candidate_first_pcm": 5.496, "stall_note": 5.497, "stall_first_pcm": 6.104, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 6.786, "expert_req": 5.497, "expert_resp": 15.729, "relay_synth_start": 15.73, "relay_first_pcm": 16.563, "relay_synth_end": 83.571, "first_any_pcm": 5.496, "first_answer_pcm": 16.563, "session_end": 84.589}, "ttfa_answer_s": 12.663, "ttfa_any_s": 1.596}
{"id": "q0524", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2565787960, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "分压电路的原理是什么？", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0524.wav", "input_sha256": "9041d8d0d09801aedb3910612edd66003b9535800d8e50ece31e0dc01f31e2d5", "input_samples": 27800, "input_s": 1.738, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.2789, "act": 0.9872, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "分享电脑通常指“把一台电脑的资源提供给其他设备/用户使用”。它的基本原理是： , 资源提供方 , 一台电脑把自己的资源开放出来，比如： , 文件 , 打印机 , 网络连接 , 屏幕画面 , 计算能力 , 网络连接 , 其他电脑或手机通过 局域网、互联网、蓝牙、Wi‑Fi 等方式连接到这台电脑。 , 权限控制 , 系统会设置账号、密码、访问权限，决定别人能不能访问、能访问什么。 , 通信协议 , 设备之间通过特定协议交换数据，例如： , 文件共享：SMB、FTP , 远程桌面：RDP、VNC , 网络共享：NAT、热点 , 打印机共享：IPP、SMB , 请求与响应 , 其他设备发出请求，比如“打开某个文件”或“控制桌面”； , 被分享的电脑接收请求，验证权限，然后把数据或画面传过去。 举例来说： , 文件共享：你的电脑把某个文件夹开放，别人通过网络访问这个文件夹。 , 屏幕共享/远程控制：你的电脑把屏幕画面实时编码后发送给对方，对方的鼠标键盘操作再传回你的电脑。 , 网络共享：电脑把一个网络连接转发给其他设备使用，本质上类似一个小路由器。 一句话概括： 分享电脑的原理就是通过网络和协议，把一台电脑的部分资源开放给其他设备，并用权限机制控制访问。", "expert_answer": "**分享电脑**通常指“把一台电脑的资源提供给其他设备/用户使用”。它的基本原理是：\n\n1. **资源提供方**\n   - 一台电脑把自己的资源开放出来，比如：\n     - 文件\n     - 打印机\n     - 网络连接\n     - 屏幕画面\n     - 计算能力\n\n2. **网络连接**\n   - 其他电脑或手机通过 **局域网、互联网、蓝牙、Wi‑Fi** 等方式连接到这台电脑。\n\n3. **权限控制**\n   - 系统会设置账号、密码、访问权限，决定别人能不能访问、能访问什么。\n\n4. **通信协议**\n   - 设备之间通过特定协议交换数据，例如：\n     - 文件共享：SMB、FTP\n     - 远程桌面：RDP、VNC\n     - 网络共享：NAT、热点\n     - 打印机共享：IPP、SMB\n\n5. **请求与响应**\n   - 其他设备发出请求，比如“打开某个文件”或“控制桌面”；\n   - 被分享的电脑接收请求，验证权限，然后把数据或画面传过去。\n\n举例来说：\n\n- **文件共享**：你的电脑把某个文件夹开放，别人通过网络访问这个文件夹。\n- **屏幕共享/远程控制**：你的电脑把屏幕画面实时编码后发送给对方，对方的鼠标键盘操作再传回你的电脑。\n- **网络共享**：电脑把一个网络连接转发给其他设备使用，本质上类似一个小路由器。\n\n一句话概括：  \n**分享电脑的原理就是通过网络和协议，把一台电脑的部分资源开放给其他设备，并用权限机制控制访问。**", "transcript": "分享电脑的原理是什么？\n", "asr_s": 0.59, "expert_s": 6.01, "expert_input_samples": 27800, "expert_input_s": 1.738, "expert_input_sha256": "9041d8d0d09801aedb3910612edd66003b9535800d8e50ece31e0dc01f31e2d5", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.379, "relay_synth_ms": 70612, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 438, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 438, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0524_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "b901cfee518acc6aa79a89dbe9850cf941d3f64cb8cec25a9bac72f49b47ae18", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 125.88}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0524_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "f5377f6505a2a2fcd259f05f0092e91ead9b04f7e5e4003a2b7de650c31aea51", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0524_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "97f334bd292fefaffc32bb0da727d1a3c30c1e54ba6378bcf536ec52e66d168a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.68}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.075, 1.135, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.738, 1.814, 1.874, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.737, 2.814, 2.875, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.737, 3.808, 4.547, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.737, 5.259, 5.773, 0, 16320, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.738, "last_real_feed_done": 1.814, "onset": 4.547, "gate_read_done": 4.547, "fire": 4.547, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.547, "stall_note": 4.548, "stall_first_pcm": 5.176, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.773, "expert_req": 4.548, "expert_resp": 11.152, "relay_synth_start": 11.153, "relay_first_pcm": 12.005, "relay_synth_end": 81.765, "first_any_pcm": 4.547, "first_answer_pcm": 12.005, "session_end": 82.166}, "ttfa_answer_s": 10.267, "ttfa_any_s": 2.81}
{"id": "q0549", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2953120259, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "创建一个正则表达式，匹配一个有效的英国电话号码。", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0549.wav", "input_sha256": "91590f6e98fb9e0c6c4243ea6eb8db9deb1297fee4be423fa9288e87135c0106", "input_samples": 71800, "input_s": 4.487, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.6351, "act": 0.9997, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "一个较常用的英国电话号码正则表达式是： 它可以匹配例如： 如果你希望稍微严格一些，要求号码以英国常见区号/手机号段开头，可以用： 说明： , +44 是英国国际区号 , 0 是英国本地拨号前缀 , 7 开头通常是手机号码 , 1、2、3 等常用于固定电话或非地理号码 , 允许号码中包含空格 注意：英国电话号码格式比较复杂，正则只能做格式校验，不能保证号码真实存在。", "expert_answer": "一个较常用的英国电话号码正则表达式是：\n\n```regex\n^(?:(?:\\+44\\s?|0)(?:\\d\\s?){9,10})$\n```\n\n它可以匹配例如：\n\n```text\n+44 7911 123456\n07911 123456\n020 7946 0958\n+44 20 7946 0958\n01632 960960\n```\n\n如果你希望稍微严格一些，要求号码以英国常见区号/手机号段开头，可以用：\n\n```regex\n^(?:(?:\\+44\\s?|0)(?:1\\d{3}|2\\d|3\\d{2}|7\\d{3}|8\\d{2})(?:\\s?\\d){6,7})$\n```\n\n说明：\n\n- `+44` 是英国国际区号\n- `0` 是英国本地拨号前缀\n- `7` 开头通常是手机号码\n- `1`、`2`、`3` 等常用于固定电话或非地理号码\n- 允许号码中包含空格\n\n注意：英国电话号码格式比较复杂，正则只能做**格式校验**，不能保证号码真实存在。", "transcript": "创建一个正则表达式，匹配一个有效的英国电话号码。\n", "asr_s": 0.68, "expert_s": 5.73, "expert_input_samples": 71800, "expert_input_s": 4.487, "expert_input_sha256": "91590f6e98fb9e0c6c4243ea6eb8db9deb1297fee4be423fa9288e87135c0106", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 20667, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 7, "feed_lag_max_ms": 613, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 1558, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0549_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "95db217fd1452195410fbbbfb53b57945525637d58c166536b8d69f41870dbb2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 37.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0549_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "4cc0d7b2909d6c55c5a3f990f0912d8569088fbbefc55e29ec2bd60ffbf76d11", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0549_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "ba23224a24611e3574ed0e98ce204edd014886b1529e053eb71699fc2ead26bf", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 8.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.069, 1.125, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.077, 2.139, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.073, 3.128, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.072, 4.13, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 4.487, 4.563, 5.22, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.487, 6.179, 6.954, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.487, 7.033, 7.803, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.487, 7.882, 8.649, 0, 24000, 0], [8, 0, 8.488, 8.725, 9.448, 0, 24000, 0], [9, 0, 9.488, 9.588, 10.225, 0, 24000, 0], [10, 0, 10.488, 10.566, 11.467, 0, 24000, 0], [11, 0, 11.488, 11.559, 12.397, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 4.487, "last_real_feed_done": 4.563, "onset": 5.22, "gate_read_done": 5.22, "fire": 5.22, "candidate_first_pcm": 5.22, "stall_note": 5.221, "stall_first_pcm": 6.101, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 12.397, "expert_req": 5.221, "expert_resp": 11.631, "relay_synth_start": 12.397, "relay_first_pcm": 13.196, "relay_synth_end": 33.064, "first_any_pcm": 5.22, "first_answer_pcm": 13.196, "session_end": 33.469}, "ttfa_answer_s": 8.709, "ttfa_any_s": 0.732}
{"id": "q0560", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4226797605, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Who was the first entomologist to describe _Amata leucacma_?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0560.wav", "input_sha256": "840e4b0b3cb40232d16cddef8de40e25cb0058b12eeaec207cf8d105a6a34de8", "input_samples": 56000, "input_s": 3.5, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.9329, "act": 0.9999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The species is most likely Amata lucerna — not “Amada lucacma.” It was first described by Alfred Ernest Wileman in 1910, originally as Syntomis lucerna. (nic.funet.fi)", "expert_answer": "The species is most likely **_Amata lucerna_** — not “Amada lucacma.” It was first described by **Alfred Ernest Wileman** in **1910**, originally as **_Syntomis lucerna_**. ([nic.funet.fi](https://www.nic.funet.fi/pub/sci/bio/life/insecta/lepidoptera/ditrysia/noctuoidea/arctiidae/ctenuchinae/amata/?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "Who was the first entomologist to describe Amada lucacma?\n", "asr_s": 0.55, "expert_s": 57.54, "expert_input_samples": 56000, "expert_input_s": 3.5, "expert_input_sha256": "840e4b0b3cb40232d16cddef8de40e25cb0058b12eeaec207cf8d105a6a34de8", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 56.932, "relay_synth_ms": 8372, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 135, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 135, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0560_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "e26f815945ebf82c181c8ece1750d7d7cd277904e2f80b448165f9854375a298", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 14.76}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0560_alwa